--------------- Library Dependencies ---------------
BabyKeySmash targets Ubuntu 22.04 / 24.04+ systems , you can get the
required packages with :

sudo apt install cmake g++ pkg-config libx11-dev libglew-dev libopencv-dev libasound2-dev libvorbis-dev

Optionally , for spoken letters and numbers ( the --speech option ) :

sudo apt install espeak-ng

The optional asset regeneration tools ( tools/make_textures.py ,
tools/import_sounds.sh ) additionally use :

sudo apt install python3-pil python3-numpy fonttools ffmpeg


--------------- Compilation ---------------
To compile the project open a terminal , cd to the root of the project and run

cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build -j$(nproc)

You can then try the application without installing anything using

./run.sh              ( or ./run.sh --greek for Greek letters )


--------------- Installation of current version ---------------
If you want to install the app ( it apt-get installs the dependencies and
compiles automatically ) , run

./install.sh

without sudo , your password is asked when the dependencies are installed and
when the files are copied to the system ( running the whole installer as root
would leave a root owned build/ directory behind ) ..

This installs the babykeysmash binary to /usr/bin and the assets
( shaders , textures , sounds , hook scripts ) to /usr/share/babykeysmash ,
after that you can start it from anywhere with :

babykeysmash
babykeysmash --greek                  ( Greek letters )
babykeysmash --speech                 ( speak letters and numbers aloud )
babykeysmash --minutes 20             ( sleepy scene after 20 minutes )
babykeysmash --moon-phase 0.5         ( force a full moon in that scene )
babykeysmash --volume 50              ( half volume for sounds and speech )
babykeysmash --simplebg               ( calm blue to black gradient , no webcam )
babykeysmash --background sea         ( pin one background , see below )
babykeysmash --webcam wobble          ( pin one webcam effect )
babykeysmash --voice f3               ( voice variant , implies --speech )
babykeysmash --list-shaders           ( list every effect and voice option )
babykeysmash --help                   ( all options )

Effects that are not pinned rotate every 3 minutes , while playing a parent
can also switch them live with Ctrl+Shift+B ( background ) and Ctrl+Shift+W
( webcam effect ) . New effects are added by dropping a ShaderToy style file
named shaders/background_NAME.frag , shaders/webcam_NAME.frag or
shaders/sleepy_NAME.frag in place , no rebuild needed .

The installation also adds a BabyKeySmash entry with a teddy bear icon to
the applications menu .


--------------- Uninstallation of current version ---------------
./uninstall.sh

This removes /usr/bin/babykeysmash and /usr/share/babykeysmash


--------------- Hook scripts ---------------
If they are executable , scripts/on_start.sh runs at startup ,
scripts/on_sleep.sh once when playtime ends and the sleepy scene begins ,
and scripts/on_exit.sh on every exit path . The bundled examples dim and
recolour an RGB keyboard with polychromatic-cli , edit them for your own
hardware or remove the execute bit to disable them .


--------------- Quitting the application ---------------
The window is deliberately hard for a toddler to close , a parent can quit by
holding Escape for 3 seconds , pressing Ctrl+Shift+Q , or typing the word
quit ( or closeapplication ) . As a last resort : pkill babykeysmash
